ISATTY(3)                      P32W Unix                       ISATTY(3)

NAME
       isatty - test whether a descriptor is a terminal

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>

       int isatty(int fd);

DESCRIPTION
       isatty returns 1 if the file descriptor fd refers to a
       terminal (/dev/tty0, /dev/tty1, /dev/tty), else 0. It asks
       for the terminal's modes with gtty (the TIOCGETP ioctl(2))
       and reports whether that worked.

       stdio uses it to decide whether stdout is line-buffered;
       programs use it to decide whether to prompt or to draw a
       screen.

RETURN VALUE
       1 or 0. When it returns 0, errno is ENOTTY (or EBADF if fd is
       not open).

EXAMPLES
       if (isatty(0))
           fputs("> ", stdout);

SEE ALSO
       stty(1), ioctl(2), stdio(3)

BUGS
       There is no ttyname: a program cannot learn which terminal it
       has from the descriptor alone.
